# tools/agent_container/profiles/workstation.env -- TEMPLATE. The workstation's local-model server, reached
# over the LAN from homelab-server. PLACEHOLDER values below (2026-09-29): a separate bake-off
# (tools/local_llm/bakeoff.py, docs/plans/2026-09-29-local-model-transition-PLAN.md section 9's "Serving
# simplification") is choosing between Ollama / Unsloth Studio / llama-swap right now and will drop the real
# BASE_URL/MODEL/CONTEXT here once it lands -- do not treat these numbers as final.
#
# Whichever server wins the bake-off MUST listen on the LAN (not just 127.0.0.1 -- today's llm.sh binds
# --host 127.0.0.1, which is UNREACHABLE from this container on a different machine) and SHOULD take an API
# key where the chosen server supports one (plan section 9, last paragraph). Until that lands, this profile
# points at the workstation's current LAN IP and the same port tools/local_llm/llm.sh already serves on
# (LLM_PORT, default 8080); TOKEN_VAR is left unset because llama-server does not enforce one today -- `llm`
# falls back to the same dummy "local" token tools/local_llm/llm.sh's own cmd_claude uses.
BASE_URL=http://192.168.0.68:8080
TOKEN_VAR=
MODEL=local
CONTEXT=65536
KIND=local
